From 702442d0b6b97b846ca5e6fa7a6071ef70449e32 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 16:27:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] Link libhegel into hypothesis-native and expose its C ABI
 to Python

libhegel is the native Rust engine behind the Hegel property-based testing
libraries: generation, shrinking, the example database and the run loop,
behind a C ABI (the hegel_* extern "C" functions of the hegeltest-c crate).
This links that crate statically into hypothesis-native and adds a thin
PyO3 surface over the parts needed to drive a run from Python: contexts and
settings (Engine), the run loop (Run / next_test_case), the typed draw
primitives, spans and collection sizing on a test case, completion, run
results with reproduce blobs, and replaying a blob as a standalone test
case. It is an experiment towards sharing one engine, not public API.

The wrappers are Send + Sync: libhegel locks its handles internally and the
GIL serialises every call, and Hypothesis's test suite drops providers from
threads other than the one that created them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_016mTrLpQ8SJg9RC9F1GH9Ac
